=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  - Data sources (web useNotifications + useTranslation): bound through the P1/S8 seam
    NotificationFilterSource -> NotificationFilterModel. The web bar is a CONTROLLED
    component — its parent owns NotificationFilters + merges the onChange patches. The
    native model holds the controlled filter state, echoes each patch locally
    (optimistic), and forwards it to the host via NotificationFilterChangeSink (web
    onChange). The source pushes the parent's filters + the vehicle/rule options +
    load/freshness status. No HTTP in the view.
  - Composition (web FilterBar + Select x2 + SearchInput + RangePicker + ActiveFilterChips):
      • FilterBar      -> responsive control row (severity chips line + pickers/search).
      • Severity chips -> 3 multi-select toggles (info/warn/critical) with SF Symbols
                          (lucide Info/AlertTriangle/AlertOctagon -> info.circle/
                          exclamationmark.triangle/exclamationmark.octagon) + status-token
                          tints (blue/amber/rose -> statusInfo/statusWarning/statusDanger);
                          web aria-pressed -> .isSelected trait; web role=group aria-label.
      • Vehicle/Rule   -> native Menu pickers (web <Select>) with the "All vehicles"/
                          "All rules" entry + a checkmark on the current value.
      • SearchInput    -> magnifying glass + bound field (prompt = web searchPlaceholder)
                          + clear button; edits route through setQuery (trim-to-nil parity).
      • RangePicker    -> from/to DatePicker fields emitting ISO yyyy-MM-dd; both set and
                          unset render (clear button / set affordance), never a blank box.
      • ActiveFilterChips -> removable "{label}: {value}" tokens (web order severity,
                          vehicle, rule, search, from, to) + Clear all.
  - States (ALL rendered, each with a #if DEBUG preview + model unit test):
      loading (option fetch, skeleton bar) · empty (no vehicles+rules -> friendly
      ContentUnavailableView) · error (fetch failed -> Retry) · content (full controlled
      bar) · stale (freshness chip + "Reconnecting…" banner + ONE auto-refresh, re-armed
      on live) · offline (cached options kept + "Offline…" banner + offline chip).
  - i18n (P1/S10): web keys preserved verbatim — notifications.inbox.filter.{allVehicles,
    allRules, severity, severity.info/warn/critical, vehicle, rule, searchLabel, from, to,
    searchPlaceholder}; native chrome namespaced under the same prefix (title/noneActive/
    activeCount/clearAll/removeFilter/clearSearch/loading/empty/error/retry/live/stale/
    offline/banners). Every code-referenced literal key (25) is declared in the catalog;
    the 3 dynamically-built severity keys are declared; referenced \ declared = empty.
    NO English string literals in native code (all via NotificationFilterStrings facade +
    Text(verbatim:)). The lone "Placeholder" substring is the web-derived key name
    `searchPlaceholder`, carried on a `// parity:allow web i18n key name, not a stub` line
    (same disposition as 0106 SessionListSection).
  - Accessibility: VoiceOver labels on every interactive element — severity chips
    (label + selected trait), vehicle/rule pickers (label + value), search field + clear,
    date fields (label + value) + clear, active chips (combined + remove), retry; the bar
    carries a combined summary (title + active-filter count); Dynamic-Type system fonts
    (Font.TS); reduce-motion honored (TSFadeIn + TSSkeleton).
  - Telemetry (P1/S11): NotificationFilterModel.start() emits view.opened with surface
    slug "NotificationFilterBar" exactly once (OSLogNotificationFilterTelemetry default;
    prod app injects the shared diagnostics adapter). Unit-tested (start twice -> 1 emit).

